Written for whichever agent picks this up next: opencode, antigravity, cursor, cline,
windsurf, zed or claude. Nothing here assumes a particular tool.

## What's happening right now

Three days of work on **why fleet launchers keep breaking**, which became `fleet-gate/` —
continuous invariants that run on a schedule instead of when someone remembers to type a
script name.

Branch: **`main`**, clean, everything pushed. (`feat/fleet-gate` still exists locally and
on origin; it is fully merged and can be deleted.)

The headline finding shapes everything else: **the fleet was never short of verification
tools — several were actively lying.** Six cases in two days of a tool reporting success
while checking nothing, three of them introduced *during* this work. That is why every
gate now has to prove it examined something (`coverage.py`).

The second finding, from yesterday: **the port allocator built to prevent collisions
created four of them in one afternoon**, because it consulted `WEBAPP_PORTS.md` and the
configs and nothing else. Docker compose files, running containers and native listeners
all claim ports too. Read `operations/PORT_OCCUPANCY.md` before touching any port.

