## Context the next agent needs

**Read `standards/AGENT_READING_ORDER.md` first.** It is the single source for what to
read in what order, and every IDE's rules file now points at it.

What `fleet-gate/` contains and why:

| Tool | Answers |
|---|---|
| `fleet_lock.py` | Port contract from the 190 configs. 0 errors (was 16) |
| `claim_ports.py` | **The only sanctioned way to take a port.** Checks registry + configs + compose + running containers |
| `compose_ports.py` | Compose/container/native occupancy, collisions, ghost containers |
| `migrate_port.py` | Moves a port everywhere it is named (10-24 places per repo). Dry run by default |
| `start_integrity.py` | Launchers that contradict or ignore their config |
| `health_probe.py` | What is actually listening and answering right now |
| `heartbeat.py` | Scheduled jobs that stopped running or started failing |
| `standards_audit.py` | Retired/rival/stale standards; regenerates the index |
| `agent_context.py` | Whether all seven IDEs actually receive the standards |
| `coverage.py` | **Whether a gate examined anything at all** |
| `nightly.ps1` | Runs the lot at 03:30 as `Fleet-Nightly-Gate` |

Four conventions that will otherwise surprise you:

- **Findings ratchet.** `baseline.json` holds accepted debt with dates; gates fail only on
  *new* breakage. A gate red from day one gets ignored, which defeats it.
- **Coverage is enforced.** A gate examining 0 units, or >50% fewer than last run, is a
  failure regardless of its exit code.
- **Batch limits are real.** `agent_context.py --apply` refuses more than 5 targets. This
  fleet has twice been broken by one blind pass (100+ `build.ps1`, 63 spec files).
- **The nightly gate shards cold starts** — 1/7 of repos per night, chosen by day-of-year.
  A repo you expect it to have tested may simply not have been in last night's shard.
  Check before blaming it, as I nearly did for six orphaned frontends whose real cause was
  the watchdog being blind to `node.exe`.

Traps that cost hours here, all now hard rules in `standards/AGENTS.md` §9:

- **BUG-031** — Bash heredocs intermittently write nothing. Use the Write tool.
- **BUG-039** — inline `python - <<'PY'` silently mangles backslash escapes.
  `"D:\Dev\repos\x"` becomes `D:` + `\D` + `ev` + CR + `epos` + CR + `x`. One case deleted
  dict entries while staying valid Python with a clean lint. Use Edit and Write. I hit this
  **twice in one session after writing the rule.**
- **Deleting or renaming a repo does not stop its containers.** Five containers from the
  deleted `games-app` repo ran for an unknown period holding seven fleet ports and blocking
  its successor `ai-games-collection` from starting. `compose_ports.py --running` now
  reports these as ghosts. `docker compose down` *before* retiring anything containerised.

